ild_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "11.7.2 (/workspace/pi-check/cache2/bin/omp/bd5868075aeeec220c745ea9f5716cfc14a96d1d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Pytest isn't installed, so I'll run the tests directly.\nThe shell seems to be removing leading whitespace, so I'll run it from a script file.\nI fixed the bug in `ledger/currency.py`. All 4 tests in `tests/test_totals.py` and the one in `tests/test_report.py` now pass. Pytest isn't installed here, so I ran each test function directly with `python3` instead of through pytest.\n\n**Cause:** `to_cents` did `int(amount * 100)`. Floats can't store most decimal prices exactly, so `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.9999\u2026`, and `int()` cuts it down to `1998`. Prices like 0.29 and 4.35 hit the same problem. Because every total is built from `to_cents`, the subtotal, tax and discount tests all came out a cent short.\n\n**Fix:** `to_cents` now converts the amount through `Decimal(str(amount))`. That reads the float as it prints (`\"19.99\"`), and the result is then rounded to whole cents, with halves rounding up. Results I checked: `19.99 \u2192 1999`, `0.29 \u2192 29`, `4.35 \u2192 435`, `-19.99 \u2192 -1999`.\n\n**Behaviour change:** amounts with fractions of a cent are now rounded instead of cut off, so `1.005` gives `101` where it used to give `100`. For prices given to the cent the old code was meant to return the same number, so this only affects inputs with more than two decimal places.